      "rerank_score_norm": 0.6466252166212592,
      "final_score": 0.7000434693723917,
      "text": "Risk of bias was assessed using the Effective Practice and Organization of Care (EPOC) risk-­ of-­ bias tool. 31 Two reviewers (JP and MM) assessed the risk of bias independently, with conflicts resolved through discussion or involvement of a third reviewer (RD). RCTs were ranked as having low risk, being unclear, or having high risk of bias across nine domains (i.e., random sequence generation, allocation concealment, similarity of baseline outcome measurements, similarity of baseline characteristics, incomplete outcome data, knowledge of the allocated interventions adequately prevented during the study, protection against contamination, selective outcome reporting, and other risk of bias) and the overall risk of bias was derived. Risk-­ of-­ bias judgments for each domain across studies were summarized using risk-­ of-­ bias graphs and summaries. Unpublished studies were considered at high risk of bias.",
